        "thought_text": "Calculate the net effect of jumps by observing that each pair of jumps (a right jump followed by a left jump) results in a net movement of (a - b). If k is even, the frog completes k/2 pairs of jumps. If k is odd, the frog completes (k-1)/2 pairs of jumps and makes one additional right jump. Therefore, the final position can be calculated as ((k // 2) * (a - b)) + (a if k % 2 == 1 else 0).",
